CAVEAT:  Three parts of the management-filter surface were not measured by this case.
         1. `ssh server allow-users` and `ssh server deny-users` exist on this DUT, and
            the DUT already carries `ssh server allow-users manager`.  They were not
            exercised.  To prove a deny through them you must try a login that must
            fail, and this platform locks an account after 5 failed logins.  That filter
            works per account, so a clean negative test would have to attack an account
            that exists.  The DUT has one privileged account.  The risk of locking it was
            not worth a limb that adds nothing to the two statements of TPS 6.1.1.
         2. `service telnet ip|ipv6` and `service ssh ip|ipv6`, the filter that selects
            an address family, exist on this DUT and were not exercised here.
         3. IPv6 management filtering was not tested.  Every leg above used IPv4.
